1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,970
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:03,680
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,040
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:05,910 --> 00:00:07,280
(PR Director's Office)

5
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:08,610
(Episode 38)

6
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:12,320
Can't you get Ms. Park away
from Seok Jin?

7
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:13,750
To a nursing home or...

8
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,650
No, a mental hospital.

9
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:16,960
Just lock her up
in a place like that.

10
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:19,490
Kang Hae Ra,
I told you not to cross the line.

11
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:24,030
If she weren't so borderline,
she'd be committed.

12
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,330
It's so annoying.

13
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:44,920
Seok Jin, it's not what you think.

14
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:13,810
(Kang Hae Ra)

15
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,250
Darn it!

16
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,460
What am I going to do?

17
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:28,190
What if Seok Jin and I
actually end up breaking up?

18
00:01:28,730 --> 00:01:31,900
I told you your big mouth
would get you into trouble.

19
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:34,430
I've told you time and time again.

20
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:37,900
To Chief Cha,
So Yeon is a vulnerability,

21
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:40,540
but she's also someone
you must never mess with.

22
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:42,040
I know that.

23
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:45,910
Shouldn't I be
his biggest weakness, though?

24
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:48,410
I'm the one who's with Seok Jin,
not his mom.

25
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,380
So why do I always come second?

26
00:01:50,950 --> 00:01:54,050
To make matters worse, now I feel
like I'm losing to Ko Eun Seol.

27
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:57,390
Do you really...

28
00:01:58,020 --> 00:01:59,420
want to have Chief Cha?

29
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:00,690
Of course.

30
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,900
I need Seok Jin to make
my life picture-perfect.

31
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:08,900
It's too late
to win his heart anyway.

32
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,570
Chief Cha didn't pick you
simply because he loves you.

33
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:14,240
You know that too.

34
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:15,870
Then what am I supposed to do?

35
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,210
A relationship
where you use each other.

36
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:20,980
Just come clean about it.

37
00:02:21,550 --> 00:02:23,280
You want me to openly admit that?

38
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:24,420
Yes.

39
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:27,820
Trying to win him over as a woman
won't get you anywhere.

40
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,120
Then what?

41
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:31,420
Go to him
as Cheongma's official successor.

42
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:35,290
Then win him over for good.
I'll help you get him.

43
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:42,770
From the budget proposal
to the beneficiary list,

44
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,300
it's clear Eun Seol pulled
an all-nighter getting this ready.

45
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,810
You're absolutely right.

46
00:02:49,070 --> 00:02:50,810
It isn't just basic job training.

47
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:52,980
Pairing it
with psychological support...

48
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:54,480
is really innovative.

49
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,210
For any educational program,

50
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:58,680
not giving up must come first.

51
00:02:58,850 --> 00:02:59,920
As expected,

52
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,450
this really shows
what experience brings to the table.

53
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:06,360
Let's keep this momentum going...

54
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:08,230
and make the scholarship program
a success.

55
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:12,560
Of course, within Cheongma Group,

56
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:16,370
there are voices of concern
regarding our scholarship program.

57
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:18,100
The truth is,

58
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:21,340
even the CEO
doesn't look on it kindly.

59
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:26,780
But let's do our best
until the very end.

60
00:03:27,010 --> 00:03:28,010
- Sure.
- Got it.

61
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:30,450
Shall we wrap up
today's meeting here?

62
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:37,620
Secretary Choi, you can go ahead
and get back to work.

63
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:39,590
Yes, I will.

64
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:44,330
That reminds me.

65
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:47,970
Won't the directors who were away
on business trips be back today?

66
00:03:48,370 --> 00:03:51,240
Yes. Director Jung and
Director Hwang are both coming in.

67
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:52,470
Then,

68
00:03:52,470 --> 00:03:55,740
could you print out the proposal
and deliver it to them?

69
00:03:56,270 --> 00:03:57,810
Sure, I'll get on it.

70
00:04:10,090 --> 00:04:12,690
(Director Jung Ji Min)

71
00:04:21,170 --> 00:04:22,800
(Director Jung Ji Min)

72
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:36,450
(Please show your support
for this board meeting.)

73
00:04:36,450 --> 00:04:37,480
(Sincerely, Kang Young Hoon)

74
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:41,220
Within Cheongma Group,

75
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:45,020
there are voices of concern
regarding our scholarship program.

76
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:47,030
The truth is,

77
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:49,690
even the CEO
doesn't look on it kindly.

78
00:05:22,630 --> 00:05:23,660
Then...

79
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:26,430
Does this mean Secretary Choi is
on CEO Kang's side?

80
00:05:27,570 --> 00:05:28,570
No way.

81
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,340
He's Director Joo's
executive secretary.

82
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:35,510
And Ms. Joo assists the Chairman
right by her side.

83
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:41,380
If you need help in the future,
feel free to contact me anytime.

84
00:05:42,210 --> 00:05:46,480
And keep me posted on the progress
of the scholarship program.

85
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,890
I'm sure there will be things
I can help with from the side.

86
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:59,360
Eun Seol, do you want
to get lunch together?

87
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:01,530
It's my treat today.

88
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:08,170
Sounds good, lunch it is.

89
00:06:13,310 --> 00:06:15,850
I finally get to have lunch
with you, Eun Seol.

90
00:06:16,650 --> 00:06:19,250
You kept playing hard to get.

91
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:25,690
What do you want to eat?
It'll be on me today.

92
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:28,430
What's this?

93
00:06:30,030 --> 00:06:31,230
What are you two doing together?

94
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,730
Eun Seol and I were going out
for lunch.

95
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,800
Exactly. Why her of all people?

96
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:38,400
- Look.
- Do we really have to...

97
00:06:40,170 --> 00:06:42,010
explain that to you, Ms. Kang?

98
00:06:43,070 --> 00:06:44,080
What?

99
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:48,580
When a superior asks you something,
you answer right away.

100
00:06:50,110 --> 00:06:53,020
As I told you last time,
my superior...

101
00:06:53,990 --> 00:06:55,490
is Director Joo Mi Ran.

102
00:06:59,990 --> 00:07:03,390
Is Ms. Joo the only superior
you have here?

103
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,330
Hey, Ko Eun Seol.

104
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:10,100
Is there any guy
you don't flirt with?

105
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:15,340
What is it about you that has men
flocking to you like this?

106
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:18,940
- You're nothing.
- I know, right?

107
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:22,080
Looks like I have a hidden charm
even I wasn't aware of.

108
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:24,180
A charm that you lack, Ms. Kang.

109
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:29,190
You're so full of yourself.

110
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:33,960
What do you want to eat?

111
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:36,330
Let's decide on the way.

112
00:07:51,410 --> 00:07:54,050
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

113
00:07:56,110 --> 00:07:58,520
Seok Jin, are you busy?

114
00:08:01,820 --> 00:08:04,690
I snapped yesterday
because I was furious.

115
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:07,830
No, even so,
I shouldn't have said those things.

116
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:10,190
I lost my temper and snapped.

117
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:15,430
I'm really, really sorry, okay?

118
00:08:16,730 --> 00:08:20,640
If she weren't so borderline,
she'd be committed?

119
00:08:22,310 --> 00:08:23,840
If my mother had been any sicker,

120
00:08:23,910 --> 00:08:26,810
you would've had her locked away
in a mental hospital.

121
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:28,480
No, absolutely not.

122
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:30,180
I only said that because I snapped.

123
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:32,350
You know how it is.

124
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:35,390
Just acting tough for no reason.
That's all it was.

125
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:37,820
I lost my cool...

126
00:08:37,890 --> 00:08:40,320
and totally lashed out
in front of the Director.

127
00:08:42,190 --> 00:08:44,960
Is using a sick person to act tough
really the best you can do?

128
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:49,630
My mom?

129
00:08:51,570 --> 00:08:53,700
After my dad died, the shock caused
her mental state to decline.

130
00:08:56,170 --> 00:08:58,940
And you'd actually put
someone that sick in a psych ward?

131
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:02,480
Forget it.

132
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,580
Why am I even talking to you?
Just go.

133
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:18,260
Secretary Choi, you mostly help
Director Joo with her work, right?

134
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:20,300
Yes.

135
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:21,770
I'm her executive secretary.

136
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:27,340
Do you also take orders
from the CEO or anyone else?

137
00:09:29,270 --> 00:09:30,980
Of course not.

138
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:33,210
I'm Director Joo's
executive secretary.

139
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:35,780
Right.

140
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,790
But why do you ask?

141
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:48,760
It looked like you and Ms. Kang
were on a similar subject earlier.

142
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:55,800
Have you had
any other run-ins with Ms. Kang?

143
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:58,970
The day I came in for my interview,

144
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:02,240
Ms. Kang and I were together
when the elevator broke down.

145
00:10:02,270 --> 00:10:03,740
I saw her briefly then.

146
00:10:04,910 --> 00:10:05,910
But...

147
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,750
she seemed like
just the kind of person I hate.

148
00:10:10,550 --> 00:10:12,480
Why? How so?

149
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:18,490
An incompetent brat born
with a silver spoon in her mouth,

150
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:22,560
throwing her weight around
like she earned it.

151
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:26,500
That's who she came across as.

152
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:30,530
You know,

153
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,170
people who haven't achieved
a single thing on their own...

154
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,210
and just throw
their parents' weight around?

155
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:37,510
I absolutely despise them.

156
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:47,220
Oh, I see. You're a lawyer.

157
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:51,060
Last time, some old lady
was looking for Joo Ae Sook too.

158
00:10:54,090 --> 00:10:57,430
Thanks for making time
on such short notice.

159
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:58,660
Not at all.

160
00:10:58,660 --> 00:11:01,000
It's for an investigation,
so of course I should help.

161
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,230
Thank you.

162
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,810
So, when that class was admitted,

163
00:11:07,810 --> 00:11:10,210
there was only one student
named Joo Ae Sook?

164
00:11:10,210 --> 00:11:11,210
That's right.

165
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:13,810
If you look here...

166
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:20,790
Among the students
admitted that year,

167
00:11:21,090 --> 00:11:22,290
she was the only Joo Ae Sook.

168
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:27,390
(Joo Ae Sook)

169
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:33,830
Didn't anyone with that name
drop out or get expelled?

170
00:11:34,070 --> 00:11:35,070
No.

171
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:38,440
If there were,
the records would still be here,

172
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,240
but there's not a single document.

173
00:11:40,870 --> 00:11:43,440
There was only one Joo Ae Sook.

174
00:11:44,610 --> 00:11:45,610
I see.

175
00:11:49,010 --> 00:11:54,620
(Joo Ae Sook)

176
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:02,930
The guardian for Kim Jin Seong
in Ward 62...

177
00:12:02,990 --> 00:12:05,460
Ms. Park So Yeon, please come in.

178
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:10,230
(Neurologist Choi Ji Woon)

179
00:12:10,770 --> 00:12:12,240
Come on in, So Yeon.

180
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:15,810
Hello.

181
00:12:21,210 --> 00:12:22,210
Auntie.

182
00:12:23,350 --> 00:12:25,320
- Are you just getting here?
- Where's Mom?

183
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:27,720
She just fell asleep.

184
00:12:28,590 --> 00:12:30,250
You took Mom
to the hospital today, right?

185
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:33,760
Yes. And your mom really liked it.

186
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:36,730
- Really?
- The facilities there are nice,

187
00:12:36,990 --> 00:12:39,730
and above all,
the doctor is so kind.

188
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:42,430
So when the doctor
asked her questions,

189
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,400
your mom answered them very clearly.

190
00:12:44,970 --> 00:12:47,870
You know how she tends
to withdraw at times.

191
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:49,510
Right.

192
00:12:49,610 --> 00:12:52,280
Anyway, I think we made
a good choice changing hospitals.

193
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:55,210
It seemed like
the perfect hospital for her.

194
00:12:55,710 --> 00:12:57,010
Thank you
for all your trouble today.

195
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,350
Well, I'll get going.

196
00:12:58,350 --> 00:12:59,920
- Okay, get home safely.
- Bye.

197
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:29,510
But I had no idea...

198
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:33,120
that CEO Kang
was such a sweet person.

199
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:37,620
The way he looked at Director Joo
was different from usual.

200
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:42,090
Honey, did you hear
about Assemblyman Cha?

201
00:13:42,430 --> 00:13:45,300
Assemblyman Cha? No, I haven't.

202
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:47,830
It seems he had an affair
with his secretary.

203
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:50,700
Ms. Yang told me about it
a while ago.

204
00:13:51,470 --> 00:13:55,240
He was sleeping with his secretary
of over ten years,

205
00:13:55,370 --> 00:13:57,010
and his wife caught them.

206
00:13:57,610 --> 00:13:58,810
Really?

207
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:00,950
So what happened?

208
00:14:01,050 --> 00:14:04,220
The apartments and buildings
registered under his name,

209
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:06,080
plus the land in his hometown,

210
00:14:06,450 --> 00:14:08,550
were all put in his wife's name.

211
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:13,620
His wife took all his assets,

212
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:15,960
and now he's dead broke.

213
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,100
Serves him right.

214
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:22,330
But out of consideration
for Assemblyman Cha,

215
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:24,170
it seems his wife
didn't reveal everything.

216
00:14:24,470 --> 00:14:26,870
Well, I'm not surprised.

217
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:29,140
His wife has her own reputation
to protect.

218
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:33,610
Why does her reputation matter?

219
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:37,750
Rather than barely maintaining
my own reputation like that,

220
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:40,350
I think I'd much rather see
the other person's ruin.

221
00:14:41,590 --> 00:14:43,520
I'd destroy them completely.

222
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:47,520
I'm going to sit back and watch
until they burn...

223
00:14:48,230 --> 00:14:49,960
to the ground.

224
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:52,030
Honey,

225
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:55,070
why are you so invested
in Assemblyman Cha's business?

226
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:00,100
Was I?

227
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:04,240
You're right.
You'd never do something like that.

228
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,940
I guess I got carried away.

229
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,120
(Neurologist Choi Ji Woon)

230
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:16,320
In short,
the severe trauma caused her...

231
00:15:16,390 --> 00:15:18,920
to suffer from dissociative amnesia.

232
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,630
Dissociative amnesia?

233
00:15:21,630 --> 00:15:23,660
In moments
of intense emotional pain,

234
00:15:23,730 --> 00:15:25,100
our brain hits...

235
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:27,000
the emergency stop button
for self-protection.

236
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,200
It shuts out painful memories,

237
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:33,270
reverting to a childlike state
that feels safe.

238
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:38,510
Then, what are the chances
she'll live with the mind...

239
00:15:39,010 --> 00:15:40,080
of a child forever?

240
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:42,450
No one can say for sure.

241
00:15:42,710 --> 00:15:46,350
Here, the brain cells aren't dead
or erased on a physical level.

242
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:49,020
So, you can think of it...

243
00:15:49,790 --> 00:15:52,290
as memories being locked away.

244
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,530
If they're only locked away,

245
00:15:58,130 --> 00:16:01,230
does that mean the memories
could come back at any time?

246
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:05,040
Yes. Specific triggers can cause
those sealed memories...

247
00:16:05,070 --> 00:16:06,700
to come back at any moment.

248
00:16:07,070 --> 00:16:09,570
That said, every case is unique,

249
00:16:09,570 --> 00:16:11,110
so we can't say for sure
when that might happen.

250
00:16:15,110 --> 00:16:16,950
When triggered,

251
00:16:17,650 --> 00:16:19,250
those memories could return?

252
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:33,800
Chief Cha,

253
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:37,230
I'm sure this incident left you
deeply disappointed in Hae Ra.

254
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:41,410
Unbelievable.

255
00:16:41,710 --> 00:16:44,710
She sometimes speaks
without thinking like that.

256
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:48,380
Perhaps it's because
of how she was raised,

257
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,720
but it's true
that she lacks consideration.

258
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:54,750
I don't see this
as a matter of consideration.

259
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:57,250
She sounded like
she genuinely meant it.

260
00:16:58,660 --> 00:17:00,820
Had she acted on that,
it would've been illegal.

261
00:17:02,090 --> 00:17:03,660
I'm not saying she was right.

262
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:06,100
She's completely
in the wrong this time.

263
00:17:07,830 --> 00:17:09,730
I called you here because...

264
00:17:10,330 --> 00:17:12,770
I want you to use this
to your advantage.

265
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,040
Chief Cha, be honest with me.

266
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:20,740
You aren't marrying Hae Ra
thinking she's going to make...

267
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,350
a great daughter-in-law.

268
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,780
You couldn't possibly have
expected that from her anyway.

269
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:29,050
I've already given up on that.

270
00:17:29,390 --> 00:17:32,790
Even so, I didn't expect her
to be this heartless.

271
00:17:34,430 --> 00:17:38,300
I want you to be smart
about this, Chief Cha.

272
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:41,130
Given Hae Ra's nature,

273
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:43,970
she'll never be able
to truly warm up to So Yeon.

274
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:45,240
Instead...

275
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,670
Instead, Hae Ra is someone...

276
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:52,810
who can put Cheongma in your hands.

277
00:17:55,150 --> 00:17:57,710
You have to cut your losses
and take what you can get.

278
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:03,420
Chief Cha, nobody calculates gains
and losses as clearly as you do.

279
00:18:04,590 --> 00:18:05,720
Given what happened,

280
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:08,230
Hae Ra won't dare treat
So Yeon badly again.

281
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:13,300
So, please think about it
one more time.

282
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:28,710
Mom, I'm home.

283
00:18:29,110 --> 00:18:30,110
Hey.

284
00:18:31,150 --> 00:18:32,320
I'm so exhausted.

285
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:40,420
By the way, why is
this week's deposit running late?

286
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,960
What? Money for living expenses?

287
00:18:43,590 --> 00:18:44,600
That's right.

288
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:47,130
We agreed on a monthly payment...

289
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:51,030
in exchange for my silence
about Eun Seol's birth mother.

290
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:54,510
Mom, do you think it's easy
to go out and make money?

291
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:57,640
Driving work has totally dried up
lately, and it's killing me.

292
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:01,750
I should go out
and earn some myself then.

293
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,450
You got fired
from the restaurant last time,

294
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:05,720
so where else can you work?

295
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:07,850
The senior center.

296
00:19:07,850 --> 00:19:09,490
Wait, don't tell me...

297
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,760
you're going to make money
playing cards.

298
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:13,590
Like you said,

299
00:19:14,390 --> 00:19:16,760
if I get a good hand,

300
00:19:17,190 --> 00:19:19,560
I might at least win some meat
like last time.

301
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:21,330
Mom, please!

302
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:28,340
At least practice before you go.

303
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:31,140
Mom.

304
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:35,580
Let's play cards
and turn pennies into a fortune.

305
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:38,980
You used to be so good at this
back in the day.

306
00:19:39,950 --> 00:19:41,220
Why didn't I think of this?

307
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:44,760
Mom, can't I sign up
at the senior center too?

308
00:19:45,690 --> 00:19:47,020
Why don't we take this chance,

309
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:50,460
team up as a mother-son duo,
and hit the jackpot?

310
00:19:50,890 --> 00:19:53,030
You punk. Unbelievable.

311
00:19:53,330 --> 00:19:56,430
Do I have to be in handcuffs
for you to come to your senses?

312
00:19:57,230 --> 00:19:59,940
What? A mother-son card team?

313
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:03,810
Just brilliant.

314
00:20:06,410 --> 00:20:09,910
Chief Cha is really thorough
and good at his job.

315
00:20:11,150 --> 00:20:13,620
That promotional shoot
must've really paid off,

316
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:16,050
considering store sales
are up significantly.

317
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:18,120
Of course.

318
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:20,490
You did the shoot personally,

319
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:22,790
so a good response was guaranteed.

320
00:20:23,330 --> 00:20:26,800
Would a single promotional shoot
show such immediate effects?

321
00:20:27,430 --> 00:20:28,900
We're still early in the game,

322
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:32,440
so the store's strong response is
likely just from opening momentum.

323
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:36,070
Don't unnecessarily inflate
Chief Cha's ego.

324
00:20:37,170 --> 00:20:38,880
He has every right to feel proud.

325
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:42,580
Chief Cha is someone
who pulls his own weight.

326
00:20:43,010 --> 00:20:44,620
For someone like him,

327
00:20:44,620 --> 00:20:46,550
encouragement is
the best motivation.

328
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:51,390
The way you put people down
while acting like you're helping...

329
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:54,960
is secretly exhausting.

330
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:57,760
Aren't I right, Director Joo?

331
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:18,350
Right, thank you.

332
00:21:19,520 --> 00:21:23,150
It seems like you can't fall asleep lately
without having a nightcap.

333
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:27,390
Yes, sleep doesn't
come easy these days.

334
00:21:28,090 --> 00:21:30,290
My wife driving me crazy
might be why.

335
00:21:31,730 --> 00:21:34,930
The aftermath of Chairman Kim
is lasting longer than I thought.

336
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:40,300
No matter what your wife thinks,
you did the right thing, sir.

337
00:21:41,470 --> 00:21:43,770
In the end, she'll understand.

338
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:47,040
Director Joo,

339
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:50,350
despite always being at her side,
you never let her influence you.

340
00:21:51,580 --> 00:21:54,320
You remain uninfluenced,
pure, and upright.

341
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:58,490
How could I be influenced?

342
00:21:59,790 --> 00:22:02,490
Her roots and background
are different from mine.

343
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:07,330
I can neither be influenced
by the Chairman...

344
00:22:07,930 --> 00:22:09,370
nor mix with her.

345
00:22:10,970 --> 00:22:15,910
Because the roots and background
she subtly stresses...

346
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:17,810
are different from mine.

347
00:22:22,310 --> 00:22:23,610
Please get some rest then.

348
00:22:26,850 --> 00:22:27,880
Tell me.

349
00:22:28,690 --> 00:22:30,850
Have you never coveted
that position?

350
00:22:32,590 --> 00:22:35,530
You must have wanted it
at least once.

351
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,600
What good would that do?

352
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,000
Even if I wanted it,

353
00:22:44,570 --> 00:22:46,140
it's something I can never have.

354
00:23:06,020 --> 00:23:08,530
Where's the fun in pulling him in
all at once?

355
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:11,330
I need to push him away
just enough...

356
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:15,300
so the tension snaps him
right back to me.

357
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,270
Kang Young Hoon, you amuse me.

358
00:23:20,340 --> 00:23:22,210
Look at you squirming
all on your own.

359
00:23:23,470 --> 00:23:25,610
What's this,
your own personal melodrama?

360
00:23:28,650 --> 00:23:29,850
(Joo Ae Sook, 128-4 Eunpa-dong,
Guwon-gu, Haseong)

361
00:23:29,910 --> 00:23:31,450
(Taeseon Hospital:
Eunpa-ro 194-gil, Guwon-gu, Haseong)

362
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:38,820
What if Director Joo really is
Eun Seol's biological mother?

363
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:43,390
Will Eun Seol be able
to handle this truth?

364
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:52,900
But why did Director Joo
go out of her way to say...

365
00:23:53,300 --> 00:23:55,240
she's Eun Seol's mother's friend?

366
00:24:08,890 --> 00:24:09,890
You must be even busier lately...

367
00:24:09,890 --> 00:24:11,450
with all the extra work
from the scholarship foundation.

368
00:24:12,090 --> 00:24:14,760
Yes, but it's nothing
I can't handle.

369
00:24:14,830 --> 00:24:17,030
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

370
00:24:17,090 --> 00:24:19,100
Right, you don't seem
to be missing a beat.

371
00:24:21,530 --> 00:24:24,630
Also, your mother and I
have plans this evening.

372
00:24:26,340 --> 00:24:27,340
My mom?

373
00:24:27,900 --> 00:24:31,010
Yes, her caregiver said
she'd bring her here.

374
00:24:31,410 --> 00:24:32,410
Really?

375
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:34,610
Then I'll pick her up later.

376
00:24:35,010 --> 00:24:37,880
No, I'll take her home
like last time.

377
00:24:38,180 --> 00:24:40,780
Actually, I'd feel a lot better
picking her up myself.

378
00:24:41,520 --> 00:24:42,520
See you later.

379
00:24:44,890 --> 00:24:45,890
Sure.

380
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:48,460
Then I'll contact you later, sir.

381
00:24:49,790 --> 00:24:50,860
All right. Here.

382
00:25:03,170 --> 00:25:06,610
Well, it's a relief
that your mother likes the hospital.

383
00:25:07,780 --> 00:25:09,050
Thank you for setting it up.

384
00:25:10,150 --> 00:25:15,490
Above all, they said overstimulation
or any kind of instability...

385
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:17,320
isn't good for the patient.

386
00:25:18,150 --> 00:25:20,190
Take extra care
to keep your mother...

387
00:25:20,420 --> 00:25:21,860
physically and mentally stable.

388
00:25:22,860 --> 00:25:26,560
Did you happen to speak
with my mother's attending physician?

389
00:25:26,630 --> 00:25:27,630
Of course.

390
00:25:28,530 --> 00:25:31,170
I recommended that hospital
for your mom in the first place,

391
00:25:31,370 --> 00:25:32,540
so naturally I met with her doctor.

392
00:25:32,970 --> 00:25:35,210
I see. Thank you.

393
00:25:36,270 --> 00:25:39,610
Make sure she doesn't miss
her regular checkups.

394
00:25:40,810 --> 00:25:41,810
I will.

395
00:25:57,030 --> 00:25:58,090
What about our daughter?

396
00:26:01,900 --> 00:26:04,330
I heard you gave birth
to our daughter.

397
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:09,740
She died a very long time ago.

398
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:16,810
No, there's no way she died.

399
00:26:18,110 --> 00:26:20,280
The woman living next door
clearly told me...

400
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:21,650
you went to the hospital in labor.

401
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:27,660
I wonder if that hospital
is still around.

402
00:26:30,430 --> 00:26:32,300
- Hey, Mr. Kim.
- Yes?

403
00:26:32,860 --> 00:26:34,930
Can I borrow your phone
for a second?

404
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:40,840
Thanks.

405
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:47,240
(30 years ago, Guwon-gu)

406
00:26:50,010 --> 00:26:53,320
(30 years ago, OB-GYN clinic
in Guwon-gu, Haseong)

407
00:27:14,740 --> 00:27:16,210
I'm back.

408
00:27:16,670 --> 00:27:17,670
Hey, Teun Teun!

409
00:27:18,140 --> 00:27:19,880
- Taekwon.
- Taekwon!

410
00:27:20,540 --> 00:27:22,810
Head home, wash your hands,
and do your homework.

411
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:27,320
Teun Teun.

412
00:27:28,690 --> 00:27:30,790
- Come here.
- What is it, Uncle?

413
00:27:31,820 --> 00:27:34,420
How do you make peace with a friend
when they're pouting?

414
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:38,960
I do the hula dance for them.

415
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,070
- The hula dance?
- Yes, like this.

416
00:27:42,770 --> 00:27:45,940
Hula, hula. I'm sorry, okay?

417
00:27:45,970 --> 00:27:47,240
- How? Like this?
- Hula, hula.

418
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:48,770
- Yes. And then...
- Like this?

419
00:27:48,770 --> 00:27:50,410
once my friends aren't mad anymore,

420
00:27:50,910 --> 00:27:54,410
they pat my butt.

421
00:27:55,050 --> 00:27:56,850
- Your butt?
- Yes.

422
00:27:57,250 --> 00:28:00,580
That's how I know
they're not mad anymore.

423
00:28:01,990 --> 00:28:02,990
Really?

424
00:28:06,690 --> 00:28:08,690
All right. One, two, three.

425
00:28:09,090 --> 00:28:11,130
Hula, hula.

426
00:28:12,860 --> 00:28:13,930
What are you doing?

427
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:17,500
Uncle and I are trying
to cheer you up, Mom.

428
00:28:17,730 --> 00:28:19,040
Cheer me up from what?

429
00:28:19,170 --> 00:28:22,210
Teun Teun said that at kindergarten,
he does the hula dance like this...

430
00:28:22,310 --> 00:28:23,610
to cheer up his upset friends.

431
00:28:23,710 --> 00:28:24,910
So I'm copying him.

432
00:28:25,140 --> 00:28:28,380
Feel better, boss. Hula, hula.

433
00:28:28,910 --> 00:28:32,780
Mom, hurry up and pat our butts.

434
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:34,750
Your butts?

435
00:28:35,750 --> 00:28:38,920
Yes, that's how we can tell
you've stopped being mad.

436
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:43,060
Are you two kidding me right now?

437
00:28:43,360 --> 00:28:45,560
We're going to keep doing this
until you stop being mad.

438
00:28:45,660 --> 00:28:46,860
Let the customers see.

439
00:28:46,930 --> 00:28:48,630
Hula, hula.

440
00:28:48,830 --> 00:28:50,330
Stop it. Seriously.

441
00:28:50,630 --> 00:28:52,340
I said stop.

442
00:28:52,340 --> 00:28:53,800
Then hurry up and pat our butts.

443
00:28:56,140 --> 00:28:58,810
Ding, you're not mad anymore. Right?

444
00:28:59,240 --> 00:29:00,610
Come on in.

445
00:29:03,410 --> 00:29:04,480
Goodness.

446
00:29:05,050 --> 00:29:06,050
Welcome.

447
00:29:06,650 --> 00:29:08,220
Will this really work?

448
00:29:09,120 --> 00:29:12,320
People naturally go easy
on sick people.

449
00:29:12,890 --> 00:29:14,560
It might be childish,
but you don't have a choice.

450
00:29:14,690 --> 00:29:16,730
You've got to win
Chief Cha over somehow.

451
00:29:16,990 --> 00:29:17,990
But it's hot.

452
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:21,870
Just tough it out.
Faking it takes work, too.

453
00:29:24,470 --> 00:29:25,540
Fine.

454
00:29:33,140 --> 00:29:36,580
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

455
00:29:38,750 --> 00:29:39,850
Yes, Director Joo.

456
00:29:40,180 --> 00:29:42,420
Chief Cha,
are you still at the office?

457
00:29:43,490 --> 00:29:44,720
I was just about to leave.

458
00:29:45,860 --> 00:29:49,030
Then could you
go see Hae Ra right now?

459
00:29:49,430 --> 00:29:51,160
She seems to have a high fever.

460
00:29:59,940 --> 00:30:01,140
Did you enjoy the food?

461
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:03,340
It was really, really good.

462
00:30:04,270 --> 00:30:06,140
In that case,
let's come back next time.

463
00:30:06,310 --> 00:30:07,310
Really?

464
00:30:07,540 --> 00:30:11,080
Next time,
let's bring Seok Jin along.

465
00:30:15,420 --> 00:30:18,660
Seok Jin will be here
to pick us up soon.

466
00:30:19,460 --> 00:30:20,460
Got it.

467
00:30:20,620 --> 00:30:22,860
By the way, nice lady,

468
00:30:24,090 --> 00:30:25,560
can we hold hands?

469
00:30:28,030 --> 00:30:29,030
I'd love to.

470
00:30:30,570 --> 00:30:33,240
- How about we walk for a bit?
- I'd like that.

471
00:30:36,940 --> 00:30:38,910
Nice lady,
what are you doing tomorrow?

472
00:30:39,910 --> 00:30:41,440
I have to be at the office.

473
00:30:41,880 --> 00:30:44,310
As for me, I'll work on...

474
00:30:44,310 --> 00:30:46,520
that coloring book
you gave me tomorrow.

475
00:30:46,620 --> 00:30:48,620
- I'm going to draw as well.
- Really?

476
00:30:57,230 --> 00:30:59,060
- Yes?
- Seok Jin.

477
00:30:59,500 --> 00:31:00,930
I'm sick.

478
00:31:01,560 --> 00:31:02,830
I absolutely love it.

479
00:31:03,430 --> 00:31:06,240
Then, do you prefer rice tteok
for tteokbokki?

480
00:31:08,170 --> 00:31:11,040
I recommended that hospital
for your mom in the first place,

481
00:31:11,040 --> 00:31:12,180
so naturally I met with her doctor.

482
00:31:12,280 --> 00:31:13,510
Instead, Hae Ra is someone...

483
00:31:14,010 --> 00:31:17,650
who can put Cheongma in your hands.

484
00:31:23,220 --> 00:31:24,450
Okay, I'll be there.

485
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:28,120
Hurry over. I'll be waiting.

486
00:31:58,350 --> 00:32:02,390
(Taeseon Hospital)

487
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,130
The hospital is bound to know.

488
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:11,530
I'm certain my daughter is alive.

489
00:32:26,420 --> 00:32:28,320
Excuse me, can I ask you something?

490
00:32:28,790 --> 00:32:30,350
Sure, how can I help you?

491
00:32:30,620 --> 00:32:32,620
Was there a patient here...

492
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:35,860
named Joo Ae Sook?

493
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:38,330
Joo Ae Sook?

494
00:32:42,770 --> 00:32:43,770
Yes.

495
00:33:06,690 --> 00:33:10,590
(A Trap Called Desire)

496
00:33:10,790 --> 00:33:12,830
If you ever come near my daughter,

497
00:33:12,830 --> 00:33:15,260
I'll take your life that very day.

498
00:33:15,500 --> 00:33:17,500
Any relationship can end
in an instant.

499
00:33:17,500 --> 00:33:19,200
I'm the official heir of Cheongma.

500
00:33:19,670 --> 00:33:21,000
Don't you want it too, Seok Jin?

501
00:33:21,300 --> 00:33:23,410
Director Joo?
Has she been coming by...

502
00:33:23,470 --> 00:33:25,170
every day at this hour?

503
00:33:25,270 --> 00:33:28,180
Before that, a lawyer dropped by.

504
00:33:28,340 --> 00:33:30,510
He was also looking for someone
named Joo Ae Sook.

505
00:33:31,080 --> 00:33:32,080
Is that so?

506
00:33:32,080 --> 00:33:35,450
Then we'll proceed with voting
on this agenda item.

507
00:33:35,850 --> 00:33:38,250
How dare the two of them
try to screw me over?

508
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:40,560
Darn it!

509
00:33:42,160 --> 00:33:44,160
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
